,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.13575948768764667,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":94.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08345591287399379,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":66.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01792741521711634,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":31.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0023708306611445185,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":53.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.016604695570697457,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":72.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.048639998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":32.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"First Business Financial Services, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for First Business Bank that provides commercial banking products and services for small and medium-sized businesses, business owners, executives, professionals, and high net worth individuals in Wisconsin, Kansas, and Missouri. The company offers commercial real estate lending, commercial and industrial lending, asset-based lending, accounts receivable financing, equipment financing, floorplan financing, vendor financing, small business administration lending and servicing, treasury management solutions, and company retirement services. It also provides private wealth management for individuals, including creating and executing asset allocation strategies, trust and estate administration, financial planning, investment management, and access to brokerage and custody-only services, as well as private banking to private wealth clients. In addition, the company offers bank consulting services consisting of balance sheet, investment portfolio, and asset liability management services. Further, it provides commercial deposit accounts. The company was founded in 1909 and is headquartered in Madison, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David R. Seiler | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $848,564 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 349 people. Revenue per employee of $483K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $175K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["First Business Financial Servic is a small-cap financial services business with a $618M market cap on $169M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $61M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 36 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 51% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"First Business Financial Services, Inc. (FBIZ) Hit a 52 Week High, Can the Run Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3021614/first-business-financial-services-inc-fbiz-hit-a-52-week-high-can-the-run-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-52_week_high-3021614","date":"2026-11-03","tim